ce\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\19(PT reserve, SY reserve).\00\00\00\00\00\00\08reserves\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\fdForced transfer of `amount` LP from `account` to the caller, without `account`'s\0aauthorization. Callable only by the configured `RecoveryEscrow`, which verifies the issuer\0aand the target's deauthorization -- like `seize` on SY/PT/YT. Works while paused.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08seize_lp\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07account\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09get_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09is_paused\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\b0Create the pool for the market run by `principal_manager`. `admin` must be the underlying's\0aissuer authority and must authorize the call. Everything else -- underlying, SY, PT, YT,\0aoracle, config, permissioning, maturity -- is read from the manager, so the pool cannot be\0awired to a mismatched set of contracts. `time_stretch_years` (1..=20) sets how gently the\0acurve flattens; the market's remaining life must stay under 75% of it.\00\00\00\0ainitialize\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11principal_manager\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12time_stretch_years\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0alp_balance\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07account\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00QThe full pool state at the current ledger time (requires a readable oracle rate).\00\00\00\00\00\00\0apool_state\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PoolState\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0apt_address\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aset_paused\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06paused\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0asy_address\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ayt_address\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\9fMove LP between accounts. Both sides must clear the underlying's compliance and\0aPermissioning, so an LP position can never be parked with an ineligible holder.\00\00\00\00\0btransfer_lp\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00?Accrued, unclaimed swap fees in SY shares: (protocol, creator).\00\00\00\00\0caccrued_fees\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\7fThe fixed annualized yield a PT buyer locks in at the spot price, at `SCALE`:\0a`(1 / price - 1) x year / tau`. Zero at maturity.\00\00\00\00\0cimplied_rate\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\01QAdd liquidity with up to `pt_desired` PT and `sy_desired` SY shares. The first deposit sets\0athe opening price (its SY value must not exceed its PT, i.e. PT priced at or below par) and\0alocks `MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY`; later deposits are taken in the current ratio, the surplus side\0aleft with the caller. Returns `(pt_used, sy_used, lp_minted)`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dadd_liquidity\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0apt_desired\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0asy_desired\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_lp_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00**True flash-mint**: tokenize `sy_in` SY into PT + YT, keep the PT in this pool's own\0areserves (exactly as if the pool had just bought it via `swap_pt_for_sy`), and send `to`\0aonly the YT. `from` ends up paying just the *net* cost -- `sy_in` minus what the pool would\0ahave paid for that PT -- not the full `sy_in`, because the pool funds the rest of the mint\0afrom its own reserves instead of from `from`'s balance. `from` must authorize transferring\0a`max_net_cost` (not `net_cost` -- see \22why `max_net_cost` is pulled, not `net_cost`\22 below);\0aany unused portion is refunded. Reverts `SlippageExceeded` if fewer than `min_yt_out` YT\0awould be minted or the net cost would exceed `max_net_cost`.\0a\0aReturns `(yt_out, net_cost)`.\0a\0a# Why this is safe: the accounting identity\0aLet `gross` be the SY value `calc_sell_pt(yt_out)` assigns the PT the mint produces (the\0asame `gross` a real seller of that PT would face), `fee` its swap-fee component, and\0a`sy_back = gross - fee` (what a real seller would be paid). Reserves move exactly \00\00\00\0dflash_mint_yt\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_yt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cmax_net_cost\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\ffHow much of `sy_shares` `Router.add_liquidity_keep_yt` should mint (rather than swap) so\0athat the minted PT and the remaining SY land in this pool's current raw reserve ratio --\0athe exact ratio `add_liquidity`'s own proportional deposit targets.\0a\0aDeliberately **not** `zap_swap_amount`: that helper solves a different problem (buying PT\0afrom this pool at the curve price, for `add_liquidity_single_sy`'s zap), and reusing it\0ahere was found, during a later integration review, to recommend the wrong split --\0a`PrincipalManager.mint` issues PT 1:1 with the net SY shares valued at the *oracle* rate,\0anot at the curve's swap price, so balancing against the curve-swap ratio generally leaves\0aSY stranded in the subsequent `add_liquidity` call instead of being fully used.\00\00\00\00\0dkeep_yt_split\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09sy_shares\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\03QPreview the full `Router.remove_liquidity_to_underlying` round trip's SY-denominated\0alegs: `remove_liquidity`'s own proportional split for `lp_in`, then selling the PT leg\0a*against the reserves as they stand after that removal* -- not the reserves before it.\0aFound needed building the dApp-integration-requested quote for that function: a first\0aversion priced the PT sale with the plain `quote_pt_for_sy` against the pre-removal\0areserves, which overstates the real payout by exactly this removal's own price impact\0a(the real multi-call sequence necessarily sells the PT *after* `remove_liquidity` has\0aalready shrunk the reserves). Returns `(pt_out, sy_out, pt_sold_for_sy, swap_fee_shares)`;\0athe last two are `0` if `pt_out` rounds to `0` (tiny `lp_in`), matching\0a`swap_gained_pt_for_sy`'s own zero-gain tolerance rather than reverting `ZeroAmount`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dquote_lp_exit\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05lp_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00NThe curve exponent `a` at WAD (1e18) for the current time; `1e18` at maturity.\00\00\00\00\00\0dtime_exponent\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0econfig_address\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\94Sell `pt_in` PT for SY. `from` pays PT, `to` receives SY. Reverts `SlippageExceeded` if less\0athan `min_sy_out` SY (after the fee) would be received.\00\00\00\0eswap_pt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\86Buy PT with `sy_in` SY shares. `from` pays, `to` receives. Reverts `SlippageExceeded` if\0afewer than `min_pt_out` PT would be received.\00\00\00\00\00\0eswap_sy_for_pt\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\01_Flash-redeem: sell `yt_in` YT for SY in one call. The pool takes the YT, recombines it with\0a`yt_in` of its own PT reserve into SY, keeps the curve price of that PT plus the fee, and\0apays `to` the rest. Reverts `SlippageExceeded` if the payout would be below `min_sy_out`,\0aand `InsufficientLiquidity` if the recombined SY does not cover the PT's price.\00\00\00\00\0eswap_yt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05yt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0etransfer_admin\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dcurrent_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09new_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0flp_total_supply\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fmanager_address\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00EPrice a PT sale of `pt_in` PT (`amount_out` is the SY after the fee).\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fquote_pt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Quote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00+Price a PT purchase with `sy_in` SY shares.\00\00\00\00\0fquote_sy_for_pt\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Quote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\e4Preview `PrincipalManager.mint` followed by `MarketPool.swap_pt_for_sy` together (the\0aflash-mint behind `Router.swap_sy_for_yt` / `swap_underlying_for_yt`): tokenizing `sy_in`\0aSY into PT+YT at the live oracle rate and `MarketConfig`'s tokenization fee, then selling\0athe minted PT back into this same pool at the live curve price. Replicates\0a`PrincipalManager.mint`'s exact formula (ceil-rounded fee, floor-rounded notional) rather\0athan calling it, since the quote must stay read-only.\00\00\00\0fquote_sy_for_yt\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eFlashMintQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\a8Preview `swap_yt_for_sy` (the flash-redeem behind `Router.swap_yt_for_sy` /\0a`swap_yt_for_underlying`): recombining `yt_in` YT with `yt_in` PT pulled from this pool's\0aown reserve, at the live oracle rate, minus the curve-priced cost of pulling that PT.\0aMatches `swap_yt_for_sy`'s own math exactly -- see `contracts/market_factory/tests/\0acreate_market.rs`-style regression tests that assert the real swap's payout equals this.\00\00\00\0fquote_yt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05yt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Quote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0frecovery_escrow\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\009How much of `sy_in` a single-sided deposit swaps into PT.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fzap_swap_amount\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00}Burn LP the escrow already holds and send the PT/SY to the escrow itself. Escrow-only;\0aworks while paused and after maturity.\00\00\00\00\00\00\10redeem_seized_lp\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02lp\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\d7Burn `lp` and send the proportional PT and SY to `to`. Available after maturity even while\0apaused (when it is the only way out); before maturity the pool pause applies. Reverts `SlippageExceeded` below the minimums.\00\00\00\00\10remove_liquidity\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02lp\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00RPay the market creator's accrued share of swap fees, in SY shares, to the creator.\00\00\00\00\00\12claim_creator_fees\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00OPrice buying exactly `pt_out` PT: `amount_in` is the SY required, fee included.\00\00\00\00\12quote_buy_exact_pt\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Quote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\aeSell `from`'s **entire** PT balance for SY, crediting `to`. Mirrors `swap_pt_for_sy`\0aexactly except for reading the amount instead of taking it as an argument -- the same\0areason `SYWrapper.withdraw_all` exists: a caller composing this after a call whose PT\0apayout is derived mid-transaction (e.g. `remove_liquidity`) cannot safely pass that\0apayout as an explicit, pre-signed `pt_in` argument to a further `require_auth`'d call\0awithout risking `Error(Auth, InvalidAction)` if reserves move between simulation and\0areal execution; reading the balance at execution time removes that argument entirely.\0aSafe only when the caller is certain `from` holds no other PT it wants to keep separate.\00\00\00\00\00\12swap_all_pt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12underlying_address\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00SPay Principal's accrued share of swap fees, in SY shares, to the config's treasury.\00\00\00\00\13claim_protocol_fees\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\02$One-time wiring of the `RecoveryEscrow` allowed to call `seize_lp`. Settable once, never\0areassigned -- so an admin mistake here (wrong address, a stale address copied from a\0adifferent market) would otherwise be permanent. Mirroring `PrincipalManager::initialize`'s\0a`assert_topology_matches` and `RecoveryEscrow::initialize`'s own cross-check of every\0aposition's `underlying_address()`, this calls back into the given address and requires its\0aown `underlying_address()` to match this pool's underlying before accepting it. Found\0aduring audit review.\00\00\00\13set_recovery_escrow\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06escrow\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Sell only the PT `from` gained *since* `baseline` -- the PT equivalent of\0a`SYWrapper.withdraw_gained`, for the same reason: a caller composing this after a call\0awhose PT payout is derived mid-transaction (e.g. `remove_liquidity`) can safely use this\0awithout first clearing out PT it already held for an unrelated reason, unlike\0a`swap_all_pt_for_sy` which acts on the *entire* balance. Found worth building during a\0alater integration review: `withdraw_gained` existed but was only wired into one Router\0aflow, while others still used the zero-pre-existing-balance idiom and failed for any\0acaller who, for instance, simply already held PT from an earlier trade.\0a\0aTolerates a zero gain gracefully (no PT bought, or none left after a prior leg) rather\0athan reverting `ZeroAmount` the way a direct `swap_pt_for_sy(0, ...)` would -- composed\0acallers cannot always guarantee a nonzero gain (e.g. `remove_liquidity` producing no PT\0aleg). Returns `0` in that case, but still enforces `min_sy_out`: a zero gain is only\0asilently fine if\00\00\00\15swap_gained_pt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08baseline\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\f7Add liquidity from SY alone: the pool buys just enough PT with part of `sy_in` (paying the\0anormal swap fee) that the remainder and the PT match the post-swap pool ratio, then adds\0aboth. Any rounding leftover is returned. Returns `(pt_used, sy_used, lp_minted)`.\0a\0aTakes the full `sy_in` from `from` up front, at the exact value the caller authorized --\0anot a time-dependent amount derived from the curve below -- and refunds whatever of it\0agoes unused. Soroban's authorization for the nested `SYWrapper.transfer` must match that\0acall's real arguments exactly; an earlier version transferred `split + sy_used`, both\0aderived from `state_fresh()` (which reads the ledger's current timestamp), so the amount\0asigned at simulation time could differ -- by a few raw units -- from the amount computed\0amoments later at execution, and the stale signature was then rejected with\0a`Error(Auth, InvalidAction)`. `sy_in` is a plain argument, identical at simulation and\0aexecution, so transferring exactly that removes the mismatch.\00\00\00\00\17add_liquidity_single_sy\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_lp_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\02nPreview `add_liquidity_single_sy`'s own `(pt_used, sy_used, lp)` exactly -- found missing\0ain a dApp-integration review (\22no quote for the two new USDY LP functions\22), since no\0aquote for this zap existed anywhere in this protocol, not even for the plain SY-denominated\0acall this previews, let alone `Router.add_liquidity_single_underlying`, which composes it.\0aReplicates the real call's math read-only (same `zap_split`/`calc_buy_pt` bisection, same\0arounding) rather than calling it, so this stays a view. Like every quote in this protocol,\0aexact only if reserves/`total_lp` do not move between this read and the real call.\00\00\00\00\00\1dquote_add_liquidity_single_sy\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\02\00\00\001Which compliance model the underlying asset uses.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04Kind\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00WClassic Stellar asset exposed through its Stellar Asset Contract (covers SEP-8 assets).\00\00\00\00\03Sac\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00KSEP-57 (T-REX) `RWAToken`: frozen flag + identity verifier + operator RBAC.\00\00\00\00\03Rwa\00")
  (@custom "contractenvmetav0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1a\00\00\00\00")
